          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "tasks that you can do but a car cannot. You are a wonderful example of a living being. Whenever you attempt to group things around you as living or non-living, you can compare them with yourself. Which characteristics help you in differentiating yourself from a car? For instance, a car does not grow. Does it mean it is non-living? Now, which characteristics have you used to classify a car as non-living? Continue your discussion in a similar way to identify the essential characteristics of living beings."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 1,
          "bbox": [
            0.115,
            0.269,
            0.743,
            0.329
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "What are some common characteristics that make living beings very different from the non-living things? Let us learn about them."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 2,
          "bbox": [
            0.115,
            0.33,
            0.743,
            0.411
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Can we consider "
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "movement",
              "styles": [
                "bold"
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " as one of the characteristics to differentiate between the living and the non-living? List five things around you that can move on their own. Do you think that all five things that you have listed can be considered as"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 3,
          "bbox": [
            0.115,
            0.412,
            0.559,
            0.492
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "living just because they can move on their own? However, unlike animals, plants do not move from one place to another. Do you consider them as living?"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 4,
          "bbox": [
            0.115,
            0.493,
            0.559,
            0.615
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Even though plants do not move from one place to another, they do show certain types of movements. Opening of flowers is one of the examples of movement in plants. Another example of movement in plants is seen in insectivorous plants. Insectivorous"
            }
          ]
        },
